{"header":{"numFound":2967,"maxScore":16.965538,"queryTime":508,"page":1,"pageSize":10},"results":[{"authors":[{"id":"orcid_______::3d1acedaf97a5ea586945bebefad8cf0","fullName":"Samiha Ouda","name":"Samiha","surname":"Ouda","rank":1,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0002-8468-1207"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Tahany Noreldin","name":"Tahany","surname":"Noreldin","rank":2,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":null,"publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"eng","label":"English"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"2. Zero hunger"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0401 agriculture, forestry, and fisheries"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"04 agricultural and veterinary sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"15. Life on land"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"6. Clean water"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Deficit Irrigation and Water Conservation","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["In this chapter, we tackled some of the concepts and definitions used in application of deficit irrigation instead of full irrigation as a technology aims at conserving irrigation water. Both water use efficiency and water productivity are important estimators in the assessment of the effect of deficit irrigation. Water use efficiency serves as a key variable in the assessment of plant responses to water stress induced by deficit irrigation. On the other hand, water productivity is a quantitative term used to define the relationship between crop produced and the amount of water involved in crop production. This chapter also reviewed deficit irrigation strategies, which consist of sustain deficit irrigation, regulated deficit irrigation (stage-based and partial root zone irrigation), and subsurface drip irrigation. The hidden role of intercropping systems in irrigation water conservation was also discussed."],"publicationDate":"2020-01-01","publisher":"Springer International Publishing","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref","Deficit Irrigation ISBN: 9783030355852"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_14cb","label":"CLOSED","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":null,"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_dedup___::43e374d5ecda60987fcd6675f1c95a16","originalIds":["10.1007/978-3-030-35586-9_2","50|doiboost____|43e374d5ecda60987fcd6675f1c95a16","3001004850"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1007/978-3-030-35586-9_2"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":0.0,"influence":2.1746283E-9,"popularity":1.1111055E-9,"impulse":0.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C5","popularityClass":"C5"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"Agricultural Research Center","acronym":"ARC","id":"openorgs____::376e6d0b558ef408e98749239587cf98","pids":[{"scheme":"PIC","value":"998571254"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/05hcacp57"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.418376.f"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000418007673"}],"countries":[{"code":"EG","label":"Egypt"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.arc.sci.eg/"}],"communities":null,"collectedFrom":[{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"},{"key":"openaire____::5f532a3fc4f1ea403f37070f59a7a53a","value":"Microsoft Academic Graph"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1007/978-3-030-35586-9_2"}],"license":"Springer TDM","accessRight":{"code":"c_14cb","label":"CLOSED","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":null},"type":"Part of book or chapter of book","urls":["https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-35586-9_2"],"publicationDate":"2020-01-01","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}},{"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1007/978-3-030-35586-9_2"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"3001004850"}],"type":"Other literature type","urls":["https://dx.doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-35586-9_2"],"refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::5f532a3fc4f1ea403f37070f59a7a53a","value":"Microsoft Academic Graph"}},{"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"3001004850"},{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1007/978-3-030-35586-9_2"}],"type":"Other literature type","urls":["https://dx.doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-35586-9_2"],"refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::5f532a3fc4f1ea403f37070f59a7a53a","value":"Microsoft Academic Graph"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":null,"fullName":"Tadesse Melkie","name":null,"surname":null,"rank":1,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Walle Jemberu","name":null,"surname":null,"rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Amare Bitew","name":null,"surname":null,"rank":3,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":"gold","publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"und","label":"Undetermined"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0106 biological sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"water use efficiency"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"deficit irrigation"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"S"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"water management"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0401 agriculture, forestry, and fisheries"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Plant culture"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Agriculture"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"04 agricultural and veterinary sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"maize"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"yield"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"01 natural sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"SB1-1110"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Optimizing water use efficiency in maize (Zea mays L.) production through deficit irrigation in Gazhen-Fuafuat Kebele, Northwest Ethiopia","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<jats:p>Ethiopia's dominant maize production relies on rain, but growing water scarcity challenges dry season irrigation efforts. This necessitates smarter irrigation techniques to maximize water use efficiency. This study optimizes water use efficiency in maize production through deficit irrigation in Gazhen-Fuafuat kebele, Fogera woreda, Ethiopia. A field experiment was conducted during the 2019/20 dry season, comparing four irrigation levels: 55%, 70%, 85%, and 100% of crop water requirements (ETc). Findings revealed that while higher irrigation levels generally enhanced plant growth and grain yield, irrigation water use efficiency was optimized at 70% ETc. Deficit irrigation at 55% ETc proved to be suboptimal, leading to significant reductions in crop growth and grain production. Conversely, applying 70% ETc resulted in a 30% reduction in irrigation water use without compromising yield. Compared to full irrigation, deficit irrigation at 85% ETc, 70% ETc, and 55% ETc resulted in yield reductions of 8%, 13.5%, and 33.1%, respectively. However, these reductions were accompanied by water savings of 15%, 30%, and 45%, respectively, leading to corresponding increases in water use efficiency of 8%, 23.4%, and 21.9%. These results suggest that deficit irrigation practices can be effectively employed to improve water use efficiency in maize production, especially in the study area facing water scarcity. This study provides valuable insights into the potential of deficit irrigation to improve maize production in Ethiopia while conserving water resources. Therefore, by implementing deficit irrigation strategies and supporting farmers with appropriate training and resources, Ethiopia can enhance its agricultural productivity and ensure food security in the face of increasing water scarcity.</jats:p>"],"publicationDate":"2024-11-26","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref","Frontiers in Agronomy, Vol 6 (2024)"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"Frontiers in Agronomy","issnPrinted":null,"issnOnline":"2673-3218","issnLinking":null,"ep":null,"iss":null,"sp":null,"vol":"6","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_dedup___::50b0f2c39397e0882217db65dc734681","originalIds":["10.3389/fagro.2024.1490423","50|doiboost____|50b0f2c39397e0882217db65dc734681","oai:doaj.org/article:83348c46f9674fe89cf4b1dd0efecb39","50|doajarticles::437d2300ea5c57e330f76532d05acee1"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.3389/fagro.2024.1490423"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":10.0,"influence":2.491276E-9,"popularity":8.3870235E-9,"impulse":10.0,"citationClass":"C4","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C4","popularityClass":"C4"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"Bahir Dar University","acronym":"BDU","id":"openorgs____::4ad165356c6fa3302261bcd1de9ce18d","pids":[{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q4842597"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/01670bg46"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.442845.b"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100005872"},{"scheme":"PIC","value":"940270956"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100005872"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000404395951"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"57092466"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"8558358"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q4842597"}],"countries":[{"code":"ET","label":"Ethiopia"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.bdu.edu.et/"}],"communities":null,"collectedFrom":[{"key":"driver______::bee53aa31dc2cbb538c10c2b65fa5824","value":"DOAJ"},{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.3389/fagro.2024.1490423"}],"license":"CC BY","accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":"gold"},"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/10.3389/fagro.2024.1490423"],"publicationDate":"2024-11-26","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"doajarticles::cc754f6d3402bd70deea089a8b4bb255","value":"Frontiers in Agronomy"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}},{"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.3389/fagro.2024.1490423"}],"accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":"gold"},"type":"Article","urls":["https://doaj.org/article/83348c46f9674fe89cf4b1dd0efecb39"],"publicationDate":"2024-11-01","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"doajarticles::cc754f6d3402bd70deea089a8b4bb255","value":"Frontiers in Agronomy"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"driver______::bee53aa31dc2cbb538c10c2b65fa5824","value":"DOAJ"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":null,"fullName":"Nawaz, Haq","name":"Haq","surname":"Nawaz","rank":1,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Türkay, Cengiz","name":"Cengiz","surname":"Türkay","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Akgün, İlknur","name":"İlknur","surname":"Akgün","rank":3,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::28cf27bfc7d9b4e9e7b6346501580bdc","fullName":"Şenyiğit, Ulaş","name":"Ulaş","surname":"Şenyiğit","rank":4,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0002-4864-0790"},"provenance":null}}],"openAccessColor":"gold","publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"eng","label":"English"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Research"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0401 agriculture, forestry, and fisheries"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"04 agricultural and veterinary sciences"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Enhancing water use efficiency and nutritional quality of maize fodder under deficit irrigation with microbial and potassium amendments","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["Optimizing maize fodder production under water limited conditions is essential for sustainable livestock systems facing climate induced water stress and declining soil fertility. In this two-year field study, we investigated how deficit irrigation at different maize growth stages (VT-R3, R3-R6, VE-VT) in combination with potassium fertilization (0, 50 kg ha⁻¹) and bacteria inoculation (B-, B+) influences water use efficiency and the nutritional quality of maize fodder. Data was recorded on acid detergent fiber (ADF), neutral detergent fiber (NDF), crude protein (CP), ash, hemicellulose, biological yield, water use efficiency and irrigation water use efficiency. Irrigation timing exerted the strongest influence on most traits. Late season deficit irrigation (R3-R6) increased fiber accumulation (ADF and NDF), whereas early season deficit irrigation (VE-VT) consistently reduced fiber accumulation while improving crude protein content and irrigation water use efficiency. Full irrigation produced the highest biological yield, followed by early season deficit irrigation. Potassium fertilization enhanced crude protein content and water use efficiency, particularly under water limited conditions. Bacterial inoculation significantly improved crude protein concentration, biological yield, and both water use efficiency and irrigation water use efficiency, with more pronounced effects under deficit irrigation. Overall, the results indicate that early season deficit irrigation (VE-VT) combined with potassium supplementation and bacterial inoculation represents an effective integrated strategy to improve forage biomass production and water productivity in maize; however, these practices may also increase fiber fractions, potentially reducing digestibility and voluntary intake, and therefore require careful balancing of yield gains with forage quality."],"publicationDate":"2026-02-13","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media LLC","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref","BMC Plant Biol"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"BMC Plant Biology","issnPrinted":null,"issnOnline":"1471-2229","issnLinking":null,"ep":null,"iss":null,"sp":null,"vol":"26","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_dedup___::8a919568dc87ea2eb05d36c11ee556e0","originalIds":["8335","10.1186/s12870-026-08335-x","50|doiboost____|8a919568dc87ea2eb05d36c11ee556e0","41688917","oai:pubmedcentral.nih.gov:13005382","50|od_______267::7b11836744518f127592c8c944ba0b29"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1186/s12870-026-08335-x"},{"scheme":"pmid","value":"41688917"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":1.0,"influence":2.187888E-9,"popularity":3.2428553E-9,"impulse":1.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C5","popularityClass":"C4"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"Isparta University of Applied Sciences","acronym":"Isparta University of Applied Sciences","id":"pending_org_::7c286ac2b732869f9fd36b5a20f7d5bf","pids":[{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/02hmy9x20"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000483580214"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.512219.c"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q52162257"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q52162257"}],"countries":[{"code":"TR","label":"Turkey"}],"websiteurl":null}],"communities":null,"collectedFrom":[{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"},{"key":"opendoar____::8b6dd7db9af49e67306feb59a8bdc52c","value":"Europe PubMed Central"},{"key":"opendoar____::eda80a3d5b344bc40f3bc04f65b7a357","value":"PubMed Central"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1186/s12870-026-08335-x"}],"license":"CC BY NC ND","accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":"gold"},"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/10.1186/s12870-026-08335-x"],"publicationDate":"2026-02-13","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"doajarticles::6adbe70743da6c40c84d008e1d0017fc","value":"BMC Plant Biology"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}},{"pids":[{"scheme":"pmid","value":"41688917"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1186/s12870-026-08335-x"}],"accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":"gold"},"type":"Article","urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41688917"],"refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"doajarticles::6adbe70743da6c40c84d008e1d0017fc","value":"BMC Plant Biology"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"opendoar____::8b6dd7db9af49e67306feb59a8bdc52c","value":"Europe PubMed Central"}},{"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1186/s12870-026-08335-x"}],"license":"CC BY NC ND","accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":null},"type":"Article","urls":["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13005382/","https://doi.org/10.1186/s12870-026-08335-x","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41688917/"],"publicationDate":"2026-02-13","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"opendoar____::eda80a3d5b344bc40f3bc04f65b7a357","value":"PubMed Central"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"opendoar____::eda80a3d5b344bc40f3bc04f65b7a357","value":"PubMed Central"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":true,"isGreen":true,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":null,"fullName":"Meriame Laita","name":"Meriame","surname":"Laita","rank":1,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::968c9c7432a104f4f0b2fc832112d9b6","fullName":"Rachid Sabbahi","name":"Rachid","surname":"Sabbahi","rank":2,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0002-8745-8799"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Khalil Azzaoui","name":"Khalil","surname":"Azzaoui","rank":3,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Belkheir Hammouti","name":"Belkheir","surname":"Hammouti","rank":4,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Hanae Nasri","name":"Hanae","surname":"Nasri","rank":5,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Zerhoune Messaoudi","name":"Zerhoune","surname":"Messaoudi","rank":6,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::0c6eed145521e7211d2399e5a8a9dd81","fullName":"Rachid Benkirane","name":"Rachid","surname":"Benkirane","rank":7,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0003-2431-1295"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Houssain Aithaddou","name":"Houssain","surname":"Aithaddou","rank":8,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":null,"publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"und","label":"Undetermined"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"2. Zero hunger"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0401 agriculture, forestry, and fisheries"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"04 agricultural and veterinary sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"15. Life on land"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"6. Clean water"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"12. Responsible consumption"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Optimizing water use and crop yield with deficit irrigation techniques: A comprehensive overview and case study from Morocco","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<jats:p>Water scarcity is a global challenge that threatens agricultural productivity and food security. Irrigation agriculture consumes most of the world’s freshwater resources and often suffers from low water use efficiency. To address water shortages, deficit irrigation techniques have been developed to minimize water inputs while sustaining or enhancing crop yields and quality. Deficit irrigation consists of allocating a minimum amount of water to the crop. It can be applied either for the entire growing season (sustained deficit irrigation) or for specific crop stages (regulated deficit irrigation). Another technique is partial root zone drying, which involves alternately irrigating different parts of the root system. This causes partial water stress and increases the water uptake efficiency. These techniques aim to maximize net water use efficiency by exploiting the physiological responses of crops to water stress. This paper provides a theoretical background on deficit irrigation, a review of recent studies on its effects on different crops and environments, and a case study in Morocco where sustained deficit irrigation was applied to peach trees in a semiarid region. The findings showed that sustained deficit irrigation reduced water use by 20% without affecting fruit yield or quality and increased water productivity by 33%. This paper also discusses the challenges and opportunities for implementing deficit irrigation in different contexts and provides some recommendations for future research and development.</jats:p>"],"publicationDate":"2024-01-26","publisher":"Malque Publishing","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":null,"container":{"name":"Multidisciplinary Reviews","issnPrinted":"2595-3982","issnOnline":"2595-3982","issnLinking":null,"ep":null,"iss":null,"sp":"2024074","vol":"7","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_________::6069d61d16464f88f0776cb52cb07baa","originalIds":["10.31893/multirev.2024074","50|doiboost____|6069d61d16464f88f0776cb52cb07baa"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.31893/multirev.2024074"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":5.0,"influence":2.2447542E-9,"popularity":5.1775197E-9,"impulse":5.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C4","popularityClass":"C4"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"Université Ibn Zohr","acronym":"Université Ibn Zohr","id":"openorgs____::47369cc50c2ce6e2173a32f6ece05516","pids":[{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q3551418"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/006sgpv47"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000121566183"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q3551418"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.417651.0"}],"countries":[{"code":"MA","label":"Morocco"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.uiz.ac.ma/"},{"legalName":"Mohammed V University","acronym":"Mohammed V University","id":"openorgs____::9d6dceaf5e56ef060226e4ef7faa28a0","pids":[{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q1360237"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q1360237"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"7245277"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100013010"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000121684024"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.31143.34"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/00r8w8f84"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100013010"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"7245570"}],"countries":[{"code":"MA","label":"Morocco"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.um5.ac.ma"}],"communities":null,"collectedFrom":[{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.31893/multirev.2024074"}],"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/10.31893/multirev.2024074"],"publicationDate":"2024-01-26","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"issn__online::be78c5d9df49191e4c1bc1024a4f6925","value":"Multidisciplinary Reviews"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":null,"fullName":"Zhe Li","name":"Zhe","surname":"Li","rank":1,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"jia Heng Zhang","name":"jia Heng","surname":"Zhang","rank":2,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid_pending","value":"0000-0002-1030-4644"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Chenli Zhou","name":"Chenli","surname":"Zhou","rank":3,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"tian Xie Chen","name":"tian Xie","surname":"Chen","rank":4,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Haiyan Li","name":"Haiyan","surname":"Li","rank":5,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":null,"publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"und","label":"Undetermined"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0401 agriculture, forestry, and fisheries"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"04 agricultural and veterinary sciences"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Effects of Deficit Irrigation on Photosynthetic, Water Productivity and Quality of Potato in an Arid Oasis Region","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<jats:p>In order to explore the effects of deficit irrigation on the photosynthesis, water productivity and quality of potato grown under membrane drip irrigation in the Hexi Oasis Irrigation Area. A field experiment were conducted in 2023 and 2024 to evaluate the effects of deficit irrigation on potato leaf area index, dry matter accumulation, photosynthetic characteristics, yield, quality and water use efficiency. Three deficit irrigation levels were set as following: mild deficit (55%–65% in field capacity, FC), moderate deficit (45%–55% in FC), and full irrigation (65%–75% in FC). Water deficit was exerted at potato seedling, tuber initiation, tuber bulking, and starch accumulation, while full irrigation was applied throughout potato growth period as the control (CK). The results indicated that compared with CK water deficit significantly (P&lt;0.05) reduced potato leaf area index, aboveground dry matter accumulation, photosynthesis, water consumption and yield, with the reduction increased with the severity of the water deficit increase. During tuber initiation the mild water deficit had no significant effect (P&gt;0.05) on potato yield compared to CK, and the water use efficiency and irrigation water use efficiency were significantly increased by 13.30% and 24.23% on average over two years, respectively. However, the moderate water deficit during potato seedling significantly increased the tuber starch and vitamin C contents, but significantly reduced the protein content. In addition, the comprehensive evaluation on multiple indicators using the TOPSIS method showed that the mild water deficit during potato tuber initiation matained the highest comprehensive score, performing the best in potato growth, photosynthesis, yield, quality and water use efficiency. Therefore, the mild water deficit during potato tuber initiation was regarded as the optimal deficit irrigation strategy for potato production in oasis, which could be used as the best irrigation mode for potato stable yield, water conservation, quality improvement and efficiency enhancement in the arid oasis irrigation areas.</jats:p>"],"publicationDate":"2026-01-01","publisher":"Elsevier BV","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":null,"container":null,"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_________::8d1b0dec5f8231a1f02942ea53c550b2","originalIds":["10.2139/ssrn.6516478","50|doiboost____|8d1b0dec5f8231a1f02942ea53c550b2"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.2139/ssrn.6516478"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":0.0,"influence":2.1746283E-9,"popularity":2.6085654E-9,"impulse":0.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C5","popularityClass":"C5"}},"projects":null,"organizations":null,"communities":null,"collectedFrom":[{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.2139/ssrn.6516478"}],"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.6516478"],"publicationDate":"2026-01-01","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}}],"links":null,"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":null,"fullName":"DUAN Weina","name":"Weina","surname":"Duan","rank":1,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"XU Jiatun","name":"Jiatun","surname":"Xu","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"CAO Yuxin","name":"Yuxin","surname":"Cao","rank":3,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"PENG Xiongbiao","name":"Xiongbiao","surname":"Peng","rank":4,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"CAI Huanjie","name":"Huanjie","surname":"Cai","rank":5,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":"gold","publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"chi/zho","label":"Chinese"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"water use efficiency"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Agriculture (General)"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"evapotranspiration"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0401 agriculture, forestry, and fisheries"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"04 agricultural and veterinary sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"TC801-978"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"summer maize"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"yield"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Irrigation engineering. Reclamation of wasteland. Drainage"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"deficit-rehydration"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"S1-972"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Effects of Deficit-irrigation at Different Stages on Evapotranspiration and Yield of Summer Maize","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["【Objective】 Deficit irrigation is a technology used widely in most arid and semi-arid regions to increase water use efficiency, but how to optimize the timing of and duration of the deficit remains elusive. The objective of this paper is to fill this gap for summer maize grown in the north of China. 【Method】 The field experiment compared three deficit irrigations by controlling the irrigation water amount at 100% (sufficient), 80% (moderate deficit) and 60% (sever deficit) of the potential evapotranspiration measured from a lysimeter (ETa). Each treatment irrigated the crop at emergence-jointing stage, jointing-tasseling stage, and tasseling-filling stage, respectively. Overall, there were nine treatments: moderate deficit irrigation at the jointing-filling stage (T1), severe deficit irrigation at the jointing-filling stage (T2), moderate deficit irrigation at the emergence-jointing and tasseling-filling stage (T3), moderate deficit irrigation at the emergence-tasseling stage and severe deficit irrigation at the tasseling-filling stage (T4), moderate deficit irrigation at the emergence-jointing stage and severe deficit irrigation at the jointing-tasseling stage (T5), severe deficit irrigation at the emergence-jointing and tasseling-filling stage (T6), severe deficit irrigation at the emergence-jointing stage and moderate deficit irrigation at jointing-tasseling stage (T7), severe deficit irrigation at the emergence-tasseling stage (T8), and moderate deficit at the tasseling-filling stage (T8). Sufficient irrigation in all stages was taken as the control (CK). In each treatment we measured the impact of rewatering on evapotranspiration, grain yield and water use efficiency of the crop. 【Result】 Compared with CK, deficit irrigation led to a decrease in evapotranspiration regardless of the stage it was imposed. Rewatering in T3 increased the evapotranspiration to a level comparable to that in CK. T5, T6 and T7 resulted in a permanent reduction in evapotranspiration even after rewatering. To avoid grain yield loss, the soil water content during the tasseling-filling stage should be maintained above 75% of the field capacity. The critical soil water was 50% of the field capacity, below which the water taken up by the crop was unable to sustain its growth. Deficit irrigation reduced the fruit yield by 5.85%～32.25%, compared to the CK, with T3 reducing the least (5.85%). T3 was thus most water-use efficient (2.81 kg/m3), increasing water use efficiency by 4.07% compared to CK. 【Conclusion】 Moderate water deficit at the seedling stage and full irrigation at the jointing-tasseling stage were optimal to improve water use efficiency without significantly reducing grain yield of the maize."],"publicationDate":"2022-02-01","publisher":"Science Press","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Guan'gai paishui xuebao, Vol 41, Iss 2, Pp 18-26 (2022)"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"Guan'gai paishui xuebao","issnPrinted":"1672-3317","issnOnline":null,"issnLinking":null,"ep":null,"iss":null,"sp":null,"vol":null,"edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doajarticles::5746f1a31841759b2297f9100aa91f6c","originalIds":["oai:doaj.org/article:e39a9d9197cd4cac8a3310b8bff561a6","50|doajarticles::5746f1a31841759b2297f9100aa91f6c"],"pids":null,"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":0.0,"influence":2.1746283E-9,"popularity":1.4615026E-9,"impulse":0.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C5","popularityClass":"C5"}},"projects":null,"organizations":null,"communities":null,"collectedFrom":[{"key":"driver______::bee53aa31dc2cbb538c10c2b65fa5824","value":"DOAJ"}],"instances":[{"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.13522/j.cnki.ggps.2021388"}],"accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":"gold"},"type":"Article","urls":["https://doaj.org/article/e39a9d9197cd4cac8a3310b8bff561a6"],"publicationDate":"2022-02-01","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"doajarticles::578a5a23b4133e0a7906daa0f40d3f87","value":"Guan'gai paishui xuebao"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"driver______::bee53aa31dc2cbb538c10c2b65fa5824","value":"DOAJ"}}],"links":null,"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":null,"fullName":"Qi Xu","name":"Qi","surname":"Xu","rank":1,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Xiaomei Dong","name":"Xiaomei","surname":"Dong","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::2e4cf9fadfc6e2de2897f84bf46b4686","fullName":"Weixiong Huang","name":"Weixiong","surname":"Huang","rank":3,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0002-1704-5550"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Zhaoyang Li","name":"Zhaoyang","surname":"Li","rank":4,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Tongtong Huang","name":"Tongtong","surname":"Huang","rank":5,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Zaijin Song","name":"Zaijin","surname":"Song","rank":6,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::622ff027ed246d94c0d0f16c9e730270","fullName":"Yuhui Yang","name":"Yuhui","surname":"Yang","rank":7,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0009-0000-9954-5462"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Jinsai Chen","name":"Jinsai","surname":"Chen","rank":8,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":"gold","publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"eng","label":"English"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0106 biological sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"2. Zero hunger"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"water use efficiency"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Botany"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"04 agricultural and veterinary sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"drip irrigation under film"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"15. Life on land"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"01 natural sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Article"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"6. Clean water"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"meta-analysis"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"machine learning"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"QK1-989"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0401 agriculture, forestry, and fisheries"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"trade-off analysis"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"cotton yield"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Evaluating the Effect of Deficit Irrigation on Yield and Water Use Efficiency of Drip Irrigation Cotton under Film in Xinjiang Based on Meta-Analysis","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<jats:p>Water scarcity constrains the sustainable development of Chinese agriculture, and deficit irrigation as a new irrigation technology can effectively alleviate the problems of water scarcity and water use inefficiency in agriculture. In this study, the drip irrigation cotton field under film in Xinjiang was taken as the research object. Meta-analysis and machine learning were used to quantitatively analyze the effects of different farm management practices, climate, and soil conditions on cotton yield and water use efficiency under deficit irrigation, to investigate the importance of the effects of different factors on cotton yield and water use efficiency, and to formulate appropriate optimization strategies. The results showed that deficit irrigation significantly increased cotton water use efficiency (7.39%) but decreased cotton yield (−15.00%) compared with full irrigation. All three deficit irrigation levels (80~100% FI, 60~80% FI, and 40~60% FI; FI: full irrigation) showed a significant decrease in cotton yield and a significant increase in water use efficiency. Under deficit irrigation, cotton yield reduction was the smallest and cotton water use efficiency increased the most when planted with one film, two tubes, a six-row cropping pattern, an irrigation frequency ≥10 times, a nitrogen application of 300~400 kg·ha−1, and a crop density ≥240,000 per hectare, and planted with the Xinluzhong series of cotton varieties; deficit irrigation in areas with average annual temperature &gt;10 °C, annual evapotranspiration &gt;2000 mm, annual precipitation &lt;60 mm, and with loam, sandy soil had the least inhibition of cotton yield and the greatest increase in cotton water use efficiency. The results of the random forest showed that the irrigation amount and nitrogen application had the greatest influence on cotton yield and water use efficiency. Rational irrigation based on optimal management practices under conditions of irrigation not less than 90% FI is expected to achieve a win–win situation for both cotton yield and water use efficiency. The above results can provide the best strategy for deficit irrigation and efficient water use in drip irrigation cotton under film in arid areas.</jats:p>"],"publicationDate":"2024-02-26","publisher":"MDPI AG","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref","Plants (Basel)","Plants, Vol 13, Iss 5, p 640 (2024)","Plants","Volume 13","Issue 5","Pages: 640"],"formats":["application/pdf"],"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"Plants","issnPrinted":null,"issnOnline":"2223-7747","issnLinking":null,"ep":null,"iss":null,"sp":"640","vol":"13","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":nul